    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "2A7m8",
      "name": "Spec: live + challenge behavior",
      "x": 3640,
      "y": 2200,
      "width": 1440,
      "content": "LIVE STATE (any run while it runs)\n- Source: live.json snapshot, refreshed every 15 s; 'updated N s ago' turns warning-colored past 60 s and shows 'connection lost, retrying' past 3 min.\n- Nothing is called a verdict or limit until the run ends: capacity says 'held X so far'; soak shows the raw memory curve only, and MB/h appears once there is 1 h of data after warm-up.\n- When the run ends, the page swaps to the normal report without a reload.\n\nCHALLENGE MODE (opt-in per run, perfkit config `challenge: { goal, milestones }`)\n- Rings: the outer pulse rings expand and fade once per second; their brightness follows calls answered that second. The progress arc eases to the new value on each snapshot.\n- Ringing strip: one dot per 1,000 calls answered in the last second, pulsing in.\n- Bell: at each milestone, a single bell sound (if sound is on), the milestone row turns green with its time, and the toast shows for 8 s with Share.\n- Sound is OFF by default; the toggle remembers the viewer's choice (localStorage). Respect prefers-reduced-motion: no pulses, counters update without animation.\n- Share builds the 1200x630 card for the latest milestone and links to the run.\n- Footer always shows the version, pinned images, machine counts and the command to reproduce."
    }
  ],
